{"team":"PIT","col":"#FFD84D","identity":"balanced","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":59.5,"adot":7.0,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Balanced Attack</h2><p>Their backs are a real part of the passing game \u2014 RBs see <strong>25%</strong> of targets (vs ~18%), which props up <strong>Jaylen Warren</strong>'s reception floor.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They lean on tempo \u2014 a 18% no-huddle rate (league ~11%) that inflates snap counts and everyone's volume.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 42% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>run-first</strong> (49% pass), funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Jaylen Warren</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 No Obvious Seam</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 67 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 42 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>114 rushing</strong> and <strong>250 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.39/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Aaron Rodgers","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":5,"props":{"Comp":20.89,"Att":32.13,"Pass Yds":222.16,"Pass TD":1.65,"INT":0.45,"Rush Yds":4.98},"d":{"completions":20.89,"attempts":32.13,"pass_yards":222.16,"pass_td":1.65,"interceptions":0.45,"rush_att":1.34,"rush_yards":4.98}}],"RB":[{"name":"Jaylen Warren","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":24,"props":{"Rush Att":13.93,"Rush Yds":63.8,"Tgt":3.55,"Rec":3.03,"Rec Yds":22.85},"d":{"rush_att":13.93,"r